WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.358
(slow dreamy music)

00:00:03.358 --> 00:00:07.141
- People often say,
“BANDALOOP is death-defying!"

00:00:07.141 --> 00:00:08.308
No, we're not.

00:00:09.192 --> 00:00:12.301
What we do is life-affirming.

00:00:12.301 --> 00:00:14.599
It celebrates the human spirit,

00:00:14.599 --> 00:00:18.112
and grace and beauty and courage.

00:00:18.112 --> 00:00:19.992
I'm not a daredevil.

00:00:19.992 --> 00:00:21.920
I am a dance-maker.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:24.920
(slow dreamy music)

00:00:30.861 --> 00:00:33.914
BANDALOOP is a dance company that,

00:00:33.914 --> 00:00:38.160
for 25 years now, has
been merging the worlds

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.743
of rock-climbing mountaineering

00:00:40.743 --> 00:00:43.520
with concert-stage dance.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:45.059
And bringing these worlds together,

00:00:45.059 --> 00:00:48.899
we're able to dance in the
mountains or on buildings,

00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:51.520
but in ways that activate those spaces

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:54.782
in unusual and wonderful ways.

00:00:54.782 --> 00:00:58.005
(slow music)

00:00:58.005 --> 00:01:00.047
(upbeat music)

00:01:00.047 --> 00:01:01.571
Hello, hello.

00:01:01.571 --> 00:01:03.993
I gotta give everyone hugs now.

00:01:03.993 --> 00:01:07.574
It takes a lot of work to
make a dream into reality.

00:01:07.574 --> 00:01:10.644
Doing the hard work,
finding the right people,

00:01:10.644 --> 00:01:15.364
practicing, failing,
failing, failing, succeeding.

00:01:15.364 --> 00:01:17.484
Having the tenacity to keep going

00:01:17.484 --> 00:01:21.651
and trying to make something
that's sort of an idea, real.

00:01:24.134 --> 00:01:27.913
The newest member of the
company is a young woman

00:01:27.913 --> 00:01:29.833
named Virginia Broyles.

00:01:29.833 --> 00:01:32.370
- Since I was a kid I
was always interested

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:35.212
in how people moved and
how to move my own body.

00:01:35.212 --> 00:01:37.608
- Double, two rock, two, check.

00:01:37.608 --> 00:01:38.877
- [Virginia] The more I
learned about BANDALOOP,

00:01:38.877 --> 00:01:40.050
the more it made sense to me,

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:41.970
because I'm not losing any of the dance

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:44.010
that I love so much, I'm
just getting to do it

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:47.177
in this other relationship to gravity.

00:01:48.058 --> 00:01:50.109
- [Amelia] I picked her because

00:01:50.109 --> 00:01:54.149
she has a really high
capacity to learn fast,

00:01:54.149 --> 00:01:56.341
take movement into her body,

00:01:56.341 --> 00:01:59.778
which is sort of like what I
call a physical intelligence.

00:01:59.778 --> 00:02:03.029
- The rotation and the
loft and jumping and

00:02:03.029 --> 00:02:04.621
all these things were
really exciting and fun,

00:02:04.621 --> 00:02:06.638
and then the next step is
like going on a building and,

00:02:06.638 --> 00:02:08.819
I was like, oh yeah, I really wanna do this,

00:02:08.819 --> 00:02:10.640
and then the voice is like, okay,

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:14.869
but is being on a building
gonna just be way too much?

00:02:14.869 --> 00:02:17.853
- Dance your dance, dance with each other.

00:02:17.853 --> 00:02:20.893
- [Virginia] I definitely feel adrenaline.

00:02:20.893 --> 00:02:22.739
Walking up to the wall
before performances,

00:02:22.739 --> 00:02:26.778
I get like really antsy
and excited and nervous.

00:02:26.778 --> 00:02:28.408
- [Woman On Walkie-Talkie]
Get in your places, go.

00:02:28.408 --> 00:02:29.890
- [Virginia] But once
something's been rehearsed

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:32.661
and you get that practice time in,

00:02:32.661 --> 00:02:36.828
I guess my goal is to achieve
the state of non-thinking.

00:02:39.121 --> 00:02:41.263
That's the ideal and
that's the most exciting

00:02:41.263 --> 00:02:44.103
because it just feels like pure enjoyment.

00:02:44.103 --> 00:02:48.000
- [Amelia] There you are,
hanging off the skyscraper,

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.514
and people look up and suddenly

00:02:50.514 --> 00:02:52.823
there's a stage, there's
art, there's beauty,

00:02:52.823 --> 00:02:55.080
there's grace, there's power in this site

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.893
that you overlook every day.

00:02:57.893 --> 00:03:00.476
(upbeat music)

00:03:02.743 --> 00:03:05.660
(electronic music)

